Cybersecurity News

 Hotel Wi-Fi Malware Attack

Today I read about a campaign where attackers targeted hotel Wi-Fi login systems to distribute malware.

What Happened?
- Attackers compromised hotel Wi-Fi portals.
- Guests connecting to the hotel's Wi-Fi were redirected to fake update pages.
- Victims were tricked into downloading malware disguised as software updates.
- The attack mainly relied on social engineering rather than exploiting the operating system directly.

Why It Matters
- Public Wi-Fi networks can be abused to target travelers.
- Fake software update pages are still an effective phishing technique.
- Users should only install software from official sources and verify update prompts.

Key Takeaway
Never trust unexpected software update prompts on public Wi-Fi. Always verify the source before downloading or installing anything.

